------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY (web source reproduced — Honesty Covenant #2/#5)
------------------------------------------------------------
- Data sources (web hooks -> native seams, no HTTP in the view):
    useTranslation -> ErrorDisplayStrings (P1/S10 facade, NSLocalizedString table "ErrorDisplay"
                      with web English `value:` fallbacks; resolves even before catalog folding).
    useNavigate    -> injected `onNavigateToList` closure (web `navigate(listHref)`); gates the
                      404 Back-to-list CTA by presence (web `listHref != null`).
    useOnlineStatus-> ErrorDisplayOnlineSource (P1/S8 state-holder seam); the model republishes
                      connectivity so the resolved branch tracks online state, like the web
                      re-render on `online` change.
- Branches reproduced (every one renders; web `status` decision tree, verbatim):
    404           -> FileQuestion (questionmark.folder), "{{thing}} not found"
                     (thing = resourceName ?? "Resource"), optional Back-to-list CTA.
    401 / 403     -> Lock (lock.fill), "Sign in required", always-present Sign-in CTA.
    5xx           -> Server (server.rack), "Server error", optional Retry CTA.
    network       -> AlertCircle (exclamationmark.circle.fill), role=alert, "Can't reach server",
                     optional Retry CTA.
    offline       -> WifiOff (wifi.slash), role=status (polite), "You're offline",
                     disabled "Retry when online" (web `!online || status === 0`, `disabled=isOffline`).
    no error      -> renders nothing (web `if (!error) return null`).
  Plus the web `compact` variant (tighter padding/typography for inline mutation errors).
  Scope note (Honesty Covenant #2): the generic P4 loading/empty/stale states do NOT exist in
  this terminal error renderer (it owns no fetch lifecycle — a parent feeds it the fault), so
  they are intentionally not fabricated; the "offline" state is the network-offline branch,
  reproduced in full. All real source branches ARE reproduced.
- i18n: 16 keys extracted verbatim from the web source, every one in ErrorDisplay.strings
  (error.notFound.{thingDefault,title,message,cta}, error.unauthorized.{title,message,cta},
   error.serverError.{title,message}, error.retry, error.network.{title,message,offlineTitle,
   offlineDetail,retryWhenOnline}). `{{thing}}` interpolation reproduced. NO English literals
   in Swift code (all via the facade).
- Accessibility: combined VoiceOver label (title + message) on the text block; CTA is a
  separately focusable control with its own label; web role/aria-live mapped (alert vs polite
  status); offline Retry rendered disabled (web aria-disabled); Dynamic-Type system fonts
  (Font.TS); no motion to gate (static surface).
- Telemetry (P1/S11): emits `view.opened` with surface slug "ErrorDisplay" on first appearance
  (ErrorDisplayTelemetry; os.Logger default; production injects the shared diagnostics sink).

